# SRG-APP-000151-AU-002330  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must use multifactor authentication for local
# access using privileged user accounts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000151-AU-002330
group:           V-206463
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000765
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Local privileged access to Splunk runs through the splunkd REST layer that
                 the CLI uses, and the product's one setting that extends a second factor
                 to that path is enableMfaAuthRest inside the configured multifactor vendor
                 stanza; Splunk Web certificate authentication does not cover the local
                 CLI.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
check:           authentication.conf [authentication] externalTwoFactorAuthVendor in Duo|RSA
check:           authentication.conf [authentication] externalTwoFactorAuthSettings non_empty


# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [<duo-externalTwoFactorAuthSettings-key>] enableMfaAuthRest https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Logon at the host console or over SSH is authenticated by the operating
                 system and its smart-card or PAM configuration, which Splunk cannot reach
external:        Duo or RSA enrollment and policy for the privileged accounts, held by the
                 multifactor vendor
external:        Splunk offers no PKI-based second factor for the CLI or REST path, so a
                 site standardized on PKI alone carries this part of the objective in the
                 operating system's console authentication
external:        Enforcement of the second factor on the REST interface, which lives in a
                 stanza whose name is chosen by the operator at run time; a criterion
                 addressed by conf, stanza, key and operator cannot reach a stanza named by
                 the value of another setting.

citation:        SRG-APP-000151-AU-002330 check and fix text;
                 authentication.conf.spec:1421-1427 (the vendor stanza is the one named by
                 externalTwoFactorAuthSettings), authentication.conf.spec:1568-1578
                 (enableMfaAuthRest, default false; the equivalent RSA setting is at
                 authentication.conf.spec:1718); web.conf.spec:120-132
finding:         The configured multifactor vendor stanza in Splunk authentication.conf
                 does not set enableMfaAuthRest = true, so the application accepts
                 single-factor credentials on the REST and CLI path used for local
                 privileged access, which is the only part of local access the product can
                 gate.
